#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105596 :question/id #uuid "b3be2b13-b455-5dde-accf-259c075e1e1f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4350" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-(-4)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105597 :question/id #uuid "c6f2dacc-11b0-5689-97d9-e1869c64aae1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4351" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105598 :question/id #uuid "4deee6cc-69e4-5da4-9c78-57bf6c988500" :question/math-academy-id "e-4352" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106044 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad8221b0-abe5-5ff1-bc3c-90d12161ae4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102151} {:answer/id #uuid "af030614-b019-5cb7-af82-49461aee453a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102152} {:answer/id #uuid "f7689ce5-7f20-51b0-9bf1-02cf4cfa28a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102153} {:answer/id #uuid "20089b8e-9e90-54c9-b1aa-d58c28a522ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102154} {:answer/id #uuid "415bcf68-6460-529e-98b7-2570d358ca23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "415bcf68-6460-529e-98b7-2570d358ca23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102155} :answer-field/id #uuid "e745e616-1f75-5e2e-88b5-a1da5a69b25d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "292a1bfa-7936-5037-9015-22a88ecb52f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-128472" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(9,6,1),$ $B(9,7,2),$ $C(7,5,2),$ and $D(7,8,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(9i+7j+2k)-(9i+6j+k) \\\\  & =j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(7i+5j+2k)-(9i+6j+k) \\\\  & =-2i-j+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(7i+8j+3k)-(9i+6j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-((-2)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 1)+((-2)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =2-6 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-4|=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc44dcc3-6969-5a60-8a18-95e97d112e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102441} {:answer/id #uuid "e883b87d-72f8-5f14-8f59-2baf9e4ae5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102442} {:answer/id #uuid "14d28786-6460-5a75-a3fa-c23f7eae95c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102443} {:answer/id #uuid "5cac3075-3c44-589e-b5a8-7fa80a0c376d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102444} {:answer/id #uuid "712d9e14-16ae-5193-8b95-86f2de039186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102445}] :answer-field/id #uuid "18712464-37e4-5f7a-8b58-067e22b69002" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102440}] :question/id #uuid "32fff2ee-f94f-5f06-8837-996515d03ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-18260" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a = ⟨k, 1, 1⟩$, $b = ⟨5, 0, 4⟩$, and $c = ⟨6, 2, 5⟩$ are coplanar."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91deb4db-6b2a-544a-ba74-25f888d469ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102447} {:answer/id #uuid "c29df26f-2f8c-5d14-9196-e5107c54f911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102448} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8b0a72-6c5b-5545-80b7-68d22aa15109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102449} {:answer/id #uuid "d2285774-835c-5d92-9c39-8d811ec66713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102450} {:answer/id #uuid "0a269770-4d2f-5b51-8afe-9049f4a722d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2285774-835c-5d92-9c39-8d811ec66713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102450} :answer-field/id #uuid "37b8f48f-b324-5fdc-82a9-632d1ad15e21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b990ba56-2404-5f20-a869-596a97b7f65e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18268" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨3,t,t⟩$, $q=⟨1,3,1⟩$, and $r=⟨1,1,3⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & t & t \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-t\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+t\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(3\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1)-t(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1)+t(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =24-2t-2t \\\\  & =24-4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 24-4t & =0 \\\\ t & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106135 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf3c4e57-2ad8-56ca-9a27-7faa2aaf1255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102687} {:answer/id #uuid "d07f6bfb-5502-5a87-b026-3ef84ecd878d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102688} {:answer/id #uuid "ec1ae10b-c98c-5aea-b28d-a0931aaf66da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102689} {:answer/id #uuid "4b15e493-3d4c-50d7-8e36-9379740a5e5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102690} {:answer/id #uuid "5c8d1f64-85e4-551c-8f55-38866b9af8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d07f6bfb-5502-5a87-b026-3ef84ecd878d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102688} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a8e5f2b-038e-5f94-8231-636fcf8c722e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c6409f39-73a4-56e7-9d4f-f576ba58985d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20138" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,2,-1)$, $B(2,3,1)$, $C(4,1,2)$, and $D(1,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(i+2j-k) \\\\  & =i+j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(4i+j+2k)-(i+2j-k) \\\\  & =3i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(i+4j+2k)-(i+2j-k) \\\\  & =2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 3)-(3\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 3)+2(3\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-9-9+12 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-6|=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "842559ea-e8de-579e-b0e2-e4bc6fd93411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104003} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b8cf03-23cd-55b9-a44e-0a91507aef2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104004} {:answer/id #uuid "07566dee-dcab-5b2b-aeff-bb244caaef53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104005} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf80ba1-1722-5eda-8a01-2202aeb56d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104006} {:answer/id #uuid "78cee756-b381-5b9c-8874-9a1d39a5f075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07566dee-dcab-5b2b-aeff-bb244caaef53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104005} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe2fd0b9-0fb1-5157-8647-5b6a0eebb344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "51de3e44-6cdb-5f9b-ba39-3a79c7ef7ab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-40214" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨3,5,0⟩$, $y=⟨3,2,0⟩$ and $z=⟨3,4,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-5\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot 5-4\\cdot 0)-5(3\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 0)+0 \\\\  & =30-75 \\\\  & =-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|-45|=45.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "268ade47-b758-5c24-b7aa-22cfb3ca64e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "79" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104009} {:answer/id #uuid "33efc085-6fcb-5388-bfd0-44fc6e3e74ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104010} {:answer/id #uuid "3613c7b9-5056-515a-a447-1260f03958c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104011} {:answer/id #uuid "5c78f5d1-616c-594d-9347-a9241287e620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104012} {:answer/id #uuid "64978af0-6e1b-5b99-a735-0eb0b544bee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104013}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b1e86f29-f1d4-5f29-893c-5c4c8887819e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104008}] :question/id #uuid "95dbfa01-f15a-5e2d-9d04-1a5d2fb0c75a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42052" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a = ⟨ - 3, 0,-2⟩$, $b = ⟨1, 5,-3⟩$, and $c = ⟨2,-1, 4⟩$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f850623-1cf0-5b7f-b020-c07acfebbd8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260983} {:answer/id #uuid "9baefb07-c1d1-5b54-860e-b68104387cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261224} {:answer/id #uuid "b255695f-5469-5e72-bef9-0b28e1845792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261451} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a3d805-1618-5717-aa44-a03a5852416b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261886} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d4c9d9-60a8-5e94-b5ef-2dd4a95c4889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4a3d805-1618-5717-aa44-a03a5852416b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261886} :answer-field/id #uuid "40927668-f3a3-5ce4-80d8-9ec8828fb9da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "59779a24-408f-5832-999c-31c9f5625f84" :question/math-academy-id "q-128421" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨2,2,3⟩,$ $q=⟨4,2,-1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-5,0,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1))-2(4\\cdot 3-(-5)\\cdot (-1))+3(4\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12-14+30 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|28|=28.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc0cb83-5eb1-5dd9-af9f-ee8ca5368146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260669} {:answer/id #uuid "788bb643-f360-5e75-ad92-1f1daf3b6599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260931} {:answer/id #uuid "c59fb9ed-aa8c-55a3-8bca-ec58a0283bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261618} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb90a7b-e64c-5bcf-9e83-02b231607e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261678} {:answer/id #uuid "fede5c03-7967-5771-bc19-dd1e5e5a6385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccb90a7b-e64c-5bcf-9e83-02b231607e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261678} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0a92faf-5d71-5f25-92c3-12fac1bc6f1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8f9b021c-bf51-5fc5-8b75-b8c974a0fbe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-128433" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨0,-1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,9,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,7,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}9 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0+(3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 2)+4(3\\cdot 7-2\\cdot 9) \\\\  & =14+12 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|26|=26.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002fdf74-6f71-54b2-830e-d9c31f46d601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259874} {:answer/id #uuid "2aca00cd-0b17-53b6-983e-a2657da0646e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260251} {:answer/id #uuid "700a04d5-9011-5132-bdd4-e0be0859896c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260858} {:answer/id #uuid "a765a9d3-1a6b-59c4-8235-ac04896438b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261337} {:answer/id #uuid "c020a971-5df5-5817-a759-23a1a56b9b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c020a971-5df5-5817-a759-23a1a56b9b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261573} :answer-field/id #uuid "22e9d0a6-6a14-5045-961e-92c3a61748d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "28e94f1b-b25a-5f14-a6d0-bd87b063c727" :question/math-academy-id "q-128436" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨8,0,3⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,1,1⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}k & 1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3)-(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 3)+4(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-3k+1+32 \\\\  & =33-3k \\\\  & =3(11-k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 3(11-k) & =0 \\\\ 11-k & =0 \\\\ k & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a7c5d9-8dc5-5287-9189-8dca5356aa94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260178} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed1a437-b5e4-5a5b-a1d5-378ea7dd2b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260693} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff60d17-d510-5a62-8746-39d3d4fdeede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261263} {:answer/id #uuid "c622ad11-5bd8-50ea-9342-3a5d4042082b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261620} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e3045d-1419-56b9-bd4b-6b851cebb90e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c622ad11-5bd8-50ea-9342-3a5d4042082b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261620} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c52dcf6-c646-5640-b426-05ef9c526397" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ff1c8b22-7226-5d88-9238-4a3a4ca77456" :question/math-academy-id "q-128454" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨t,t,1⟩,$ $q=⟨3,2,6⟩,$ and $r=⟨3,4,0⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =\\begin{vmatrix}t & t & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =t\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-t\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =t(2\\cdot 0-4\\cdot 6)-t(3\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 6)+(3\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-24t+18t+6 \\\\  & =-6t+6 \\\\  & =6(1-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 6(1-t) & =0 \\\\ 1-t & =0 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0735f2d3-4813-5f6a-8ebd-3180c4020c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259945} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd7650e-e217-51b4-8281-479af6811358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260132} {:answer/id #uuid "308d2e52-c1bb-5e72-989b-40a3fc41595e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260312} {:answer/id #uuid "33903820-9a8f-5e3f-9139-32338148d2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260343} {:answer/id #uuid "499d6073-74e0-579f-97bb-9cb4a8239ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dd7650e-e217-51b4-8281-479af6811358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260132} :answer-field/id #uuid "b025cca6-310c-5c80-a31c-1d52565eae81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "23db8f87-cf26-5e8b-9a16-08cc8381ac4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128456" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $a=⟨3,-1,7⟩,$ $b=⟨t,4,t⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,6,8⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 & 7 \\\\ t & 4 & t \\\\ 2 & 6 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & t \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}t & t \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{vmatrix}+7\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}t & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(4\\cdot 8-6\\cdot t)+(t\\cdot 8-2\\cdot t)+7(t\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =96-18t+8t-2t+42t-56 \\\\  & =30t+40 \\\\  & =10(3t+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 10(3t+4) & =0 \\\\ 3t+4 & =0 \\\\ t & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=-\\frac{4}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262907 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "196c7bb9-2703-5d83-8058-24be71bcb43b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260097} {:answer/id #uuid "44662d03-7907-5288-b2f2-17f084b58313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260471} {:answer/id #uuid "5d8121de-a71a-5f79-841e-03f4c4d8f85c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260679} {:answer/id #uuid "c69b8832-1644-5736-8a79-f96a8d866802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261625} {:answer/id #uuid "fba18045-5247-5864-b09c-6d2f59aad9bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44662d03-7907-5288-b2f2-17f084b58313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260471} :answer-field/id #uuid "00e3b359-0ccd-5626-ac16-03a3053097e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1edaed17-510c-5349-a80b-092dc57c864f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128475" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(7,6,4),$ $B(8,5,9),$ $C(7,4,2),$ and $D(5,7,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(8i+5j+9k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =i-j+5k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,5⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(7i+4j+2k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(5i+7j+4k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i+j \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-2))+(0\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot (-2))+5(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2-4-20 \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-22|=22.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262912 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2758af71-201a-5743-a5ec-86afd2e415e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260219} {:answer/id #uuid "2d261462-d03d-544c-a8a9-5aadec24e0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260283} {:answer/id #uuid "329c90d2-6fee-5509-8239-ab93f795292c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260332} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3acf1f-c9af-515f-b70d-f86b50febc38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260981} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd8e8e6-f4f4-53d7-b173-9afee1bb078b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebd8e8e6-f4f4-53d7-b173-9afee1bb078b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261944} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4794f4f-7acb-5b9b-a59f-bc47efacaf2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "86e3bae5-31f6-5b6c-93f8-27d7bdeaa8bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-128483" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(5,1,4),$ $B(4,1,7),$ $C(3,1,5),$ and $D(2,3,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+j+7k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+j+5k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+3k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-3i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1)-0+3((-2)\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2-12 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-10|=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "416f2b02-f671-5dac-9033-c92a97bb7433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285396} {:answer/id #uuid "66d33b0d-7ab1-5eac-8f4e-3d2df7928766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285722} {:answer/id #uuid "e258b1f3-74dd-5a16-b9ea-949bbeba773d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286849} {:answer/id #uuid "e508fab7-8c7c-5655-84d6-97881cdb4aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286884} {:answer/id #uuid "e5eaf3c4-9cd2-569f-bb87-a49a632e2001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66d33b0d-7ab1-5eac-8f4e-3d2df7928766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285722} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf368173-4107-5226-9931-f9efe2d03ed0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b2a99499-e25e-5c3a-b8fd-38e4eb5f4e8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-18259" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-3,3,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $c=⟨0,4,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3((-1)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 4-0\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =39-6+8 \\\\  & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|41|=41.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287823 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ff76ae-3310-5976-b521-37e9f161c00c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2,k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285085} {:answer/id #uuid "36a55f04-0655-55ca-bff1-1b7ac91e9f99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3,k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285297} {:answer/id #uuid "7d71d038-0b8e-53eb-98a4-4f2424b98e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285941} {:answer/id #uuid "d004be87-813b-53a7-aaa4-dec132a85008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286681} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa8a48c-b3c4-5cc9-a1a6-003916fe2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1,k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d004be87-813b-53a7-aaa4-dec132a85008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286681} :answer-field/id #uuid "08df0eaf-8693-5325-ba44-b70c3634becf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b9713970-1739-5ce7-ae00-abfb91e16a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18266" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors  $p=⟨0,-1,-{k}^{2}⟩,q=⟨2,4,8⟩$ and $r=⟨-1,-1,5⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 & -{k}^{2} \\\\ 2 & 4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+(-{k}^{2})\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0+(2\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 8)-{k}^{2}(2\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =18-2{k}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 18-2{k}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =9 \\\\ k & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-3$ or $k=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b91b1ff-04f2-5241-991f-a0cc2cfb0602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284879} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7e0a12-c398-51c0-ac5a-185f2ba8acab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285635} {:answer/id #uuid "7171ef21-9125-54d8-8548-7452920c7a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285829} {:answer/id #uuid "af7840a2-d107-597a-a2b9-cc938cae9f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286386} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5d05e0-fae6-5640-bc73-d08f6f6d4a87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7171ef21-9125-54d8-8548-7452920c7a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285829} :answer-field/id #uuid "62967656-4da8-539f-8bc8-d9d85e319b59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1d7560d3-4e5c-58e1-a4ce-975d4218030d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20145" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(2,1,2)$, $B(3,3,3)$, $C(-2,-1,3)$, and $D(4,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+3j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+j+4k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 1)-2((-4)\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1)+((-4)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-4+20+4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|20|=20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10bfef10-81ba-573e-b324-c7127dd0dcb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10bfef10-81ba-573e-b324-c7127dd0dcb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290704} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb77c768-bf57-5c30-9432-4fac33eb1964" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f4a8b31c-e171-5959-8851-e81cf194bca8" :question/math-academy-id "q-275353" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨-2,1,-3⟩$, $b=⟨-1,k,2⟩$, and $c=⟨3,-2,4⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}k & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+(-3)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & k \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2(k\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-8k-8+10-6+9k \\\\  & =k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ k-4 & =0 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26d8406f-9482-553b-b669-150af1e6419e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26d8406f-9482-553b-b669-150af1e6419e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293103} :answer-field/id #uuid "884c153a-6afe-5960-8b8a-07f28b451975" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "227e2bc0-7de3-5c22-93a6-04542a843855" :question/math-academy-id "q-280314" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(3,-2,1),$ $C(-1,4,-1),$ and $D(2,1,0).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =2i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+4j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-2i+4j+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =i+j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(8-1)+2(-4-1)+3(-2-4) \\\\  & =14-10-18 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-14|=14.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee18266d-e68c-52ab-82f3-47d654c336f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee18266d-e68c-52ab-82f3-47d654c336f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293858} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd8d3efa-1d88-5610-a5fb-f056f628a424" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0c8b632f-0961-529e-b3d4-1d020cf7c2fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-280321" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,-3,2),$ $B(4,-1,5),$ $C(-2,0,1),$ and $D(3,-2,3).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i-j+5k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j+3k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1)-2((-3)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3((-3)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(3+1)-2(-3+2)+3(-3-6) \\\\  & =12+2-27 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-13|=13.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0db0f54-7a45-5d43-9fcd-054949c78c87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0db0f54-7a45-5d43-9fcd-054949c78c87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293684} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e49acb-95ca-5b40-a0e2-ffd8b5733da3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fbb0f86b-7cc9-5ea8-b795-4408792fb13b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280670" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $y=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, and $z=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1-4-6 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37cae9e7-d969-5e06-929a-5039d5412e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37cae9e7-d969-5e06-929a-5039d5412e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293165} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6b9ddd1-8994-5843-973e-8858e59c45a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8009ac60-6b35-55bb-b7cb-31b4072308ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-280671" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,1,2⟩$, $y=⟨-3,2,0⟩$, and $z=⟨4,-2,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-2))-1((-3)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 4)+2((-3)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2+3-4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|1|=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35b3feda-548d-5212-bb14-ab63c3adb049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35b3feda-548d-5212-bb14-ab63c3adb049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293161} :answer-field/id #uuid "3654f79e-6420-50ab-9f46-330c40c4756d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "783ca205-66c5-547b-848c-076696d6e4cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-280712" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,5,0⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(30)-2(0)+3(-20) \\\\  & =30-0-60 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-30|=30.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6417e993-0593-5472-a921-eba5a037e141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6417e993-0593-5472-a921-eba5a037e141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293345} :answer-field/id #uuid "108e88d1-9385-56ac-be72-c53c0bca9938" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c8ebdcbf-5834-5ffb-a71e-6b022b6fe2f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-280716" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $x=⟨3,1,4⟩$, $y=⟨0,2,5⟩$, and $z=⟨6,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 0)-(0\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 6)+4(0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =6+30-48 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-12|=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0618fdf5-9970-590e-8185-d4fd25d3af95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0618fdf5-9970-590e-8185-d4fd25d3af95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292957} :answer-field/id #uuid "03def6c9-038a-52fb-8620-4828ee17ec9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "02a24008-f4b2-51f6-bfa2-34173306dcaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-280720" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $x=⟨2,0,k⟩$, $y=⟨1,4,3⟩$, and $z=⟨0,2,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 2)+0+k(1\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(20-6)+2k \\\\  & =28+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =0 \\\\ 28+2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =-28 \\\\ k & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153692ac-17dc-5340-8ab8-c764df7ca660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "153692ac-17dc-5340-8ab8-c764df7ca660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293019} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b34c4d0-3f40-5fab-a961-3f1c1324f59d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "61f3e6a0-31a0-537c-a9de-e6c7ae59826e" :question/math-academy-id "q-280722" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,2⟩$, and $c=⟨2,k,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (b\\times c)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k & 5\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ k & 5\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot k)-3(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2)=(20-2k)+12 \\\\  & =32-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 32-2k & =0 \\\\ -2k & =-32 \\\\ k & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2dab13-46de-5120-87e8-8117a287ba97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2dab13-46de-5120-87e8-8117a287ba97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293049} :answer-field/id #uuid "89673c8b-815d-53a8-b014-fbcc596ce325" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ee4f8503-0b7f-5200-9b9f-9ac97e166c2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280729" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,k,k⟩$, $b=⟨0,3,2⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & k & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 0)-k(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 4)+k(0\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =15+8k-12k \\\\  & =15-4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 15-4k & =0 \\\\ 4k & =15 \\\\ k & =\\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{15}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1865ae1-27be-5cb9-8458-215d6d36baf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1865ae1-27be-5cb9-8458-215d6d36baf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293871} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a9e2261-c7fc-53d6-9874-00c30b303f22" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99a0dde8-2f69-5f2c-aab5-cf49c4fd974f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99a0dde8-2f69-5f2c-aab5-cf49c4fd974f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293539} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ff6522-eece-5b68-a25a-d04312e1a764" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "85dbcbc6-7e0b-5364-ba3b-2e4b14e4021a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280735" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨4,{k}^{2},2⟩$, $b=⟨1,5,3⟩$, and $c=⟨2,1,0⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n**In ascending order:** $\\,$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}\n$\\,$\nand\n$\\,$\n$k=${{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & {k}^{2} & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-{k}^{2}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(5\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 1)-{k}^{2}(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 2)+2(1\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =4(-3)-{k}^{2}(0-6)+2(1-10) \\\\  & =-12+6{k}^{2}-18 \\\\  & =6{k}^{2}-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet the triple product equal to 0:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{k}^{2}-30 & =0 \\\\ 6{k}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =5 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if \n$k=-\\sqrt{5}$ or $k=\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295173 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8801f3a-9dfd-5e9f-8521-78d48c05cc43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8801f3a-9dfd-5e9f-8521-78d48c05cc43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293652} :answer-field/id #uuid "57b4cf71-7bea-51e2-9884-e3e9016b64cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "35b9e288-8b36-5336-a7cf-8f490e426c0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-281023" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,0,2),$ $B(3,4,5),$ $C(6,2,4),$ and $D(5,3,6).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+5k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+4j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,4,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(6i+2j+4k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =5i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨5,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(5i+3j+6k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =4i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨4,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 3)-4(5\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 4)+3(5\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2(8-6)-4(20-8)+3(15-8) \\\\  & =4-48+21 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-23|=23.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae1af4a9-9139-556a-a009-9963fb4181c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae1af4a9-9139-556a-a009-9963fb4181c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293614} :answer-field/id #uuid "bccf3ad9-32f3-5b0c-8104-4809c72ee239" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "143e14fb-6cbe-5d90-85cc-144627915d33" :question/math-academy-id "q-281025" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,0,2),$ $B(5,1,3),$ $C(4,3,5),$ and $D(3,0,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5i+1j+3k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =3k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(3\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)-1(1\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)+1(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(9)-1(3)+1(0) \\\\  & =18-3+0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|15|=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cb7e495-32de-5ba1-b91b-cfaa604be24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb7e495-32de-5ba1-b91b-cfaa604be24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293432} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaec393b-7696-58c0-adfd-28a0339820a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7ad6a5b8-f3d8-5275-887d-fa59251ace92" :question/math-academy-id "q-281029" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,1,3),$ $B(0,5,5),$ $C(3,4,5),$ and $D(2,0,2).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5j+5k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =4j+2k \\\\  & =⟨0,4,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+5k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+2k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+2k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =2i-1j-1k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}-4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-4(3\\cdot -1-2\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot -1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =28-18 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6122a148-198a-57cc-b7dd-7fcbcaac6bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6122a148-198a-57cc-b7dd-7fcbcaac6bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293328} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6bff096-9adc-55e6-b402-42dc714742c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c74fea15-7593-5e2d-a899-51b33896c8fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-281030" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(-1,0,1),$ $B(2,-3,4),$ $C(-2,-2,2),$ and $D(0,-1,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-3j+4k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =3i-3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-2j+2k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+1k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-j+5k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-(-3)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(-8+1)+3(-4-1)+3(1-(-2)) \\\\  & =-21-15+9 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-27|=27.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c1b7b71-b2b9-52b7-b3b2-a252ff8b3a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324209} {:answer/id #uuid "2f47aecc-9c32-5fd9-bb33-9b522561ab80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324348} {:answer/id #uuid "4c521838-fa08-5257-af4e-02df87616189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324598} {:answer/id #uuid "c2857d99-7846-589d-b5e9-648f4a7b08fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325641} {:answer/id #uuid "d5bb6ee2-1d36-5d99-992a-5cea026f4b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f47aecc-9c32-5fd9-bb33-9b522561ab80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324348} :answer-field/id #uuid "c18648a9-dbca-508f-b015-0d411d90c876" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "072fa115-fcc0-55b5-8eb6-62f44d05b685" :question/math-academy-id "q-40221" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-5,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,4⟩$ and $c=⟨1,1,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-5((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)-3(2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)+0 \\\\  & =25+6 \\\\  & =31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|31|=31.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09532a7b-1bde-5425-aa2a-a897fa63b438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324054} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6d850b-f14f-5354-8f2a-89eb6f418867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324329} {:answer/id #uuid "88ce51b5-6b4e-5a60-90fa-8279e2abd028" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325135} {:answer/id #uuid "9a93b40d-5533-56f2-bb93-1c0e463a14c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325288} {:answer/id #uuid "cd846ac4-5a9b-5d65-b3ce-525881f5605f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd846ac4-5a9b-5d65-b3ce-525881f5605f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325756} :answer-field/id #uuid "105ffdf3-9def-5878-8052-550f2e45a407" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6db83569-7cb0-5537-ab90-423f6f08147e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42048" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,2,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $c=⟨4,1,3⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}k & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)-2(3\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-2k-2+6 \\\\  & =-2k+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -2k+4 & =0 \\\\ 2k & =4 \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f844ee1-c259-5a95-b62b-bbd5374d3b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324887} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4abec8-a143-5cf6-aa13-c8003ec34d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325306} {:answer/id #uuid "b02ae5f9-07f7-5ad0-ab01-09d9bba0420c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325470} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e59a19-9725-5ca0-9531-7a13df7b3f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326032} {:answer/id #uuid "ff3d10eb-7d0b-5944-8d90-7dee6bddee49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f844ee1-c259-5a95-b62b-bbd5374d3b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324887} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc134bae-1f69-5a15-863b-dcc9d6d57c23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cf69007e-3a95-53fc-ae94-e7b4176da553" :question/math-academy-id "q-42050" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨1,-2,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨0,2,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 1)+2(2\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 1)+(2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-22+20+4 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|2|=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2ef31a-319f-5526-8854-d1b97cef6f67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339500} {:answer/id #uuid "9e339643-b9aa-5ec5-bb9d-d0f58d998ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340554} {:answer/id #uuid "c980250c-e65e-5d17-8ea3-88bc5b175137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340914} {:answer/id #uuid "f2befcf1-babe-5a30-94de-07cd59778c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341267} {:answer/id #uuid "f570d31c-370d-5b83-a9d2-4dd414372eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2befcf1-babe-5a30-94de-07cd59778c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341267} :answer-field/id #uuid "30f2ba25-a3d1-5f35-b797-85e2998465c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3a2d9a59-591c-58a1-9378-a824f178afc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73735" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨0,3,6⟩$, $q=⟨t,t,2⟩$, and $r=⟨-1,2,7⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ t & t & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}t & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}t & 2 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{vmatrix}+6\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}t & t \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-3(t\\cdot 7-(-1)\\cdot 2)+6(t\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot t) \\\\  & =-21t-6+12t+6t \\\\  & =-3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ -3t-6 & =0 \\\\ -3t & =6 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "480d8a6c-d976-500e-a7e2-36b07adb1298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339770} {:answer/id #uuid "92b3ca28-cec3-54f5-8108-604c09001fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340447} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ccd3d8-500a-5a10-b8dd-140f303da80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340777} {:answer/id #uuid "c7936625-73aa-5282-9707-cfefef43ada2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340898} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ddbf57-82d0-56ba-af3f-5120ce6bc488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5ccd3d8-500a-5a10-b8dd-140f303da80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340777} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9dc32f6-3810-5869-9997-de4c6edc03fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "029d2415-156a-588b-85c8-9df58fb943a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73736" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨t,1,t⟩$, $q=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and $r=⟨3,0,1⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =\\begin{vmatrix}t & 1 & t \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =t\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+t\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =t((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-1))-(2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1))+t(2\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-t-5+3t \\\\  & =2t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 2t-5 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =5 \\\\ t & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=\\frac{5}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342075 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22269750-3610-50c1-9f1a-e32029db2cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339419} {:answer/id #uuid "82067827-a66f-5c6a-aae6-789419de79b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340299} {:answer/id #uuid "826586c2-1bf6-5265-9275-8aca9ef0a3ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340301} {:answer/id #uuid "df70070c-22ea-53f2-a484-ebf2fd57d953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341114} {:answer/id #uuid "fc03c5f9-9d3d-5c25-b729-1dac1a0eaf64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82067827-a66f-5c6a-aae6-789419de79b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340299} :answer-field/id #uuid "46d6930c-5eff-59bb-a41f-2cb0e35d6542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b1acfcbc-5797-5d52-8f43-51fb0ff9335f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73744" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,1,0)$, $B(-2,1,0)$, $C(3,2,0)$, and $D(1,2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =-3i \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =2i+1j \\\\  & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+3k)-(i+j) \\\\  & =3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)-0+0 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342076 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40d26a0c-7c01-5b6a-8dbe-ae3604c79b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339707} {:answer/id #uuid "a94320ec-b8fb-55d4-958d-7f0d1f959771" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340668} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f68538-632a-565b-b512-ff8470d73e8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341125} {:answer/id #uuid "e65f7298-4237-5dfe-b5fe-c41469fbc270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341164} {:answer/id #uuid "f379ed93-ced2-52c2-a4c4-17422c45cfea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40d26a0c-7c01-5b6a-8dbe-ae3604c79b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339707} :answer-field/id #uuid "96aeb4dc-4ea9-539b-be68-45022f3c1e44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d447f611-67a9-5187-a844-7f81dc30a0cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-73745" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,-1,2)$, $B(-2,2,3)$, $C(1,1,1)$, and $D(-1,3,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+2j+3k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j+k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-i+3j-2k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+4j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot (-4)-4\\cdot (-1))-3(0\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot (-1))+(0\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12+6+4 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|22|=22.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e68b3bb-a8f2-5479-b9ed-52016f094a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339842} {:answer/id #uuid "74595172-003f-5459-ac1c-c67762230b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340167} {:answer/id #uuid "7c79963c-8405-5654-a813-6c58246f39a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340249} {:answer/id #uuid "afcfce9c-9dd3-53e7-912f-479a3e8ba88d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340733} {:answer/id #uuid "c1713077-7d22-57aa-a570-36388f38332a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74595172-003f-5459-ac1c-c67762230b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340167} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e1f964d-62df-5320-b2e6-31249877cf9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "eae017c3-e923-584f-9dc9-ad18f462f150" :question/math-academy-id "q-73746" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(0,1,2)$, $B(-1,0,1)$, $C(1,1,0)$, and $D(3,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =i-2k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-j+3k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-2))+(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-2))-(1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =4+7+2 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|13|=13.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342078 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "041ecafc-32e3-55b2-bd4d-16b2bb0a3485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339154} {:answer/id #uuid "12b4a91a-647d-55f9-aa8c-e6d3645734f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339293} {:answer/id #uuid "7833b55c-3b8d-5820-a478-1c02f596ba57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340200} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ef1d18-3b2d-548c-8803-d8c7d794cda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341193} {:answer/id #uuid "ed939920-d631-5c81-9821-0b25e67f578f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9ef1d18-3b2d-548c-8803-d8c7d794cda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341193} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f32398d-38d4-52b0-b5d4-56a201268afd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b26b4535-e272-5e94-b038-84726ee96584" :question/math-academy-id "q-73748" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(2,-1,0)$, $B(-1,2,-1)$, $C(1,1,2)$, and $D(3,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j-k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =-i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-j+k)-(2i-j) \\\\  & =i+k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-6+9+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|\\,5\\,|=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d62eb44-4e3a-5892-a344-22adca5fb4b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339674} {:answer/id #uuid "44264ce2-e3a9-5eee-be94-e13b2e0593c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339727} {:answer/id #uuid "4f8808dc-6f23-5a33-9124-c4c4fa2dbcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339852} {:answer/id #uuid "c947e433-5802-530f-8f38-59049f701448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340912} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f27876-a2cf-5204-a145-b4f7fba572a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c947e433-5802-530f-8f38-59049f701448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340912} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac0fe630-b555-5ba6-bee4-4141e867e478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed1f88a5-7f29-5728-a62d-81ac2d1ace51" :question/math-academy-id "q-73753" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(-2,1,1)$, $B(2,1,0)$, $C(1,-1,2)$, and $D(3,-2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =4i-k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j-2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =5i-3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨5,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot (-3))-0-(3\\cdot (-3)-5\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =36-1 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|35|=35.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6523e66f-3eae-532d-af4f-39b785b57f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378568} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0d16a7-95d1-5a5f-aa7e-734db7ae523b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378569} {:answer/id #uuid "9365d6aa-7405-5556-acfb-cdae2d97fb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378570} {:answer/id #uuid "03bf534f-e82e-5f46-aa2b-26e765dc8c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378571} {:answer/id #uuid "b288711d-0efe-5c03-b8d4-fcbdbce46686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03bf534f-e82e-5f46-aa2b-26e765dc8c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378571} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee88383b-1dff-5bb7-9ff0-c76d09dd0d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "df2041e4-731a-5917-8788-670168bfca15" :question/math-academy-id "q-128453" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨8,4,6⟩,$ $b=⟨8,-4,5⟩,$ and $c=⟨0,2,k⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{vmatrix}-4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{vmatrix}+6\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}8 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =8(-4\\cdot k-2\\cdot 5)-4(8\\cdot k-0\\cdot 5)+6(8\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-32k-80-32k+96 \\\\  & =16-64k \\\\  & =16(1-4k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 16(1-4k) & =0 \\\\ 1-4k & =0 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{1}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a42f150-af09-50f1-93e5-5a7ef6c3941c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378575} {:answer/id #uuid "0e61ab76-8c5d-5910-8b87-4c64f34d8f37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378576} {:answer/id #uuid "132eab41-9a12-5b05-a76e-570681089bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378577} {:answer/id #uuid "eeaa0c77-6439-57a3-810c-a0949283ed9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378578} {:answer/id #uuid "9c500f0c-3011-5638-86d3-c14893131d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c500f0c-3011-5638-86d3-c14893131d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378579} :answer-field/id #uuid "88508ed0-7bb9-51fe-90d6-2bd0fcd3f98d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "57ae3b89-c4ab-5dbf-a8d7-b1b9339d2673" :question/math-academy-id "q-128482" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,0,1),$ $B(0,-1,3),$ $C(1,-2,2),$ and $D(2,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-j+3k)-(3i+k) \\\\  & =-3i-j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-2j+2k)-(3i+k) \\\\  & =-2i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+2j+k)-(3i+k) \\\\  & =-i+2j \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3((-2)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 1)+((-2)\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1)+2((-2)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =6+1-12 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-5|=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d6275c-2c2f-59ab-b7b4-5b1eda58e833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379357} {:answer/id #uuid "b445dedd-49e6-575a-8fa2-7a20bed64a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqr